SYNTHESIS
  The abstract finite-difference packets are perfectly formal: B_j is
  exactly dual to W_j, and q0 is the alternating boundary of W.
  But the generated frontier does not follow a simple signed W1, W2, or
  B2 rule.  The robust generated witnesses are the absolute low leakage
  |W1|+|W2| and the Bonferroni4 U4 readout; this matches HYP-2722/HYP-2727.
  Therefore the HYP-2725/HYP-2727 proof order should be strengthened:
  formalize the finite-difference boundary first, then prove generated-word
  exclusion for the cheap atom-cone directions before applying the
  factorial odd L1 envelope to the high relation-support tail.
